    "paragraph": "National-Scale Multimodal Accessibility Fields from Open Geospatial Data introduces MAPPER, an open-data C++/OpenMP pipeline that processes OpenStreetMap and GTFS data with network kernel density estimation to build continuous travel-time fields for walking, biking, driving, and public transit. Evaluated near Cusco, Peru, A political ecology of reforestation in the Peruvian Andes examines how institutional dynamics and tree species choices influence tree-planting initiatives through a political ecology framework. Changing contribution of a shared neighbourhood pattern to reported sexual and non-sexual violence against women and girls in Medellín, Colombia, 2018--2022 applies a Bayesian shared-component model to 46,390 reported cases across 285 neighbourhoods to track spatial violence patterns.",
